# Use a synthetic patient and an isolated FHIR environment.

@fhirBaseUrl = {{FHIR_BASE_URL}}
@fhirAccessToken = {{FHIR_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
@identifierSystem = {{FHIR_PATIENT_IDENTIFIER_SYSTEM}}
@syntheticIdentifier = {{FHIR_SYNTHETIC_PATIENT_IDENTIFIER}}
@syntheticPatientId = {{FHIR_SYNTHETIC_PATIENT_ID}}
@sutraBaseUrl = {{SUTRA_BASE_URL}}
@sutraAccessToken = {{SUTRA_ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### FHIR capability discovery
GET {{fhirBaseUrl}}/metadata
Authorization: Bearer {{fhirAccessToken}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Exact system-and-value patient search
GET {{fhirBaseUrl}}/Patient?identifier={{identifierSystem}}%7C{{syntheticIdentifier}}&_count=2
Authorization: Bearer {{fhirAccessToken}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Patient read
GET {{fhirBaseUrl}}/Patient/{{syntheticPatientId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fhirAccessToken}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Encounter search with bounded page size
GET {{fhirBaseUrl}}/Encounter?patient={{syntheticPatientId}}&_count=50
Authorization: Bearer {{fhirAccessToken}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Runtime adapter capability discovery through SUTRA
GET {{sutraBaseUrl}}/api/v1/integrations
Authorization: Bearer {{sutraAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### SUTRA exact-identifier behavior
GET {{sutraBaseUrl}}/api/v1/patients/by-identifier/{{syntheticIdentifier}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{sutraAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Negative test: populate with a value known to be only a prefix; this must return 404.
GET {{sutraBaseUrl}}/api/v1/patients/by-identifier/{{FHIR_SYNTHETIC_PARTIAL_IDENTIFIER}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{sutraAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
